      "text": [
        "111 - وَقَالَ اَلصَّادِقُ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ: «أَرْبَعٌ مِنْ سُنَنِ اَلْمُرْسَلِينَ اَلتَّعَطُّرُ وَ اَلسِّوَاكُ وَ اَلنِّسَاءُ وَ اَلْحِنَّاءُ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.111 - Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) said:\n\"Four practices are from the traditions of the messengers: applying fragrance, using siwak (toothstick), having relations with women, and using henna.\""
        ]
      }
